Package: RosettaGBR
Title: Cross-Method Prediction for GBR Coral Cover and COTS Monitoring Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("CCIP", "BR-04 Team", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "placeholder@example.com")
Description: Prediction functions for calibration models relating different
    Great Barrier Reef monitoring methods (manta tow, ReefScan Surface,
    ReefScan Deep, RHIS, eDNA) to one another, for coral cover (Beta
    regression) and Crown-of-Thorns Starfish counts/presence (Negative
    Binomial and Binomial regression). Extends 'RosettaCOTS'
    (Foster, github.com/Scott-Foster/RosettaCOTS), which supports CCIP D-02's
    site-level calibration models, with the tow/cull-site/reef multi-level
    model set built for CCIP BR-04 (project RJFMP), and re-exports
    'RosettaCOTS's own (otherwise internal/unexported) D-02 per-model
    functions under stable names alongside them (see 'rosetta_models()').
    The BR-04 functions take a posterior-samples matrix (from the saved
    BR-04 model fits, columns alpha/beta/phi for Beta
    models or alpha/beta/r for Negative Binomial models, population-level
    only) and a vector of predictor values, and return posterior
    mean/credible-interval/prediction-interval curves; this package does not
    fit models or bundle data for them -- it is a prediction/
    calibration-curve layer only. The D-02 functions are thin pass-throughs
    to 'RosettaCOTS', which does bundle its own fitted posteriors.
